stdout | Usage: elp [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]
stdout |
stdout | Commands:
stdout |   parse-elp             Tree-sitter parse all files in a project for specified rebar.config file
stdout |   parse-all             Dump ast for all files in a project for specified rebar.config file
stdout |   eqwalize              Eqwalize specified modules
stdout |   eqwalize-all          Eqwalize all opted-in modules in a project
stdout |   eqwalize-target       Eqwalize all opted-in modules in specified buck target
stdout |   eqwalize-app          Eqwalize all opted-in modules in specified application
stdout |   build-info            Generate build info JSON file
stdout |   generate-completions  Generate shell completions
stdout |   server                Run lsp server
stdout |   lint                  Parse files in project and emit diagnostics, optionally apply fixes
stdout |   lint-compare          Diff two `elp lint --format=json` JSONL artifacts
stdout |   search                Search Erlang code by syntax-tree shape (not text) using SSR (Structural
stdout |                         Search and Replace) patterns.
stdout |   ssr                   Alias for 'search': search Erlang code structurally using SSR patterns.
stdout |   version               Print version
stdout |   shell                 Starts an interactive ELP shell
stdout |   daemon                Manage a persistent ELP daemon for fast turnaround
stdout |   explain               Explain a diagnostic code
stdout |   lint-list             List all available lint diagnostic codes
stdout |   project-info          Generate project info file
stdout |   glean                 Glean indexer
stdout |   config                Dump a JSON config stanza suitable for use in VS Code project.json
stdout |   help                  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
stdout |
stdout | Options:
stdout |   -h, --help     Print help
stdout |   -V, --version  Print version
stdout |
stdout | Global options:
stdout |       --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
stdout |       --erl <ERL>            
stdout |       --escript <ESCRIPT>    
stdout |       --no-log-buffering     
stdout |       --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
stdout |       --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
stdout |                              auto]
